Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-18 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved), but for mylib/x.step (below): a design whose own symbols and
footprints sit under a path variable of its own, MYLIB, for libs.remove,
paths.set and project.libs's vars (tests/e2e/lib-rows.spec.ts). An empty
one sheet schematic and an empty two layer board with a 40 by 30 mm outline
(the board is tests/fixtures/blank's); sym-lib-table and fp-lib-table each
hold ONE row, MyLib, of uri ${MYLIB}/x.kicad_sym and ${MYLIB}/x.pretty, so
nothing of them loads until MYLIB names the folder mylib. mylib/x.kicad_sym
holds one symbol, R_MyLib (two pins), whose footprint is MyLib:R_MyLib;
mylib/x.pretty/R_MyLib.kicad_mod is a two pad footprint whose model line
names ${MYLIB}/x.step.

mylib/x.step is R_0402_1005Metric.step copied unchanged from
kicad-packages3D at KiCad's tag 10.0.4 (Resistor_SMD.3dshapes, one resistor
body), renamed: CC BY-SA 4.0 with KiCad's libraries exception, whose license
mylib/LICENSE.md is kept beside it as kicad-packages3D ships it.

files.json lists what the e2e harness opens. The KiCad files carry no
comment (their formats have none), so this file holds their license.
